# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# Lines are chosen to be structurally distinct from their siblings. Codemark
# refuses a bookmark whose generated query matches more than one node, so a
# statement with an identically-shaped sibling is not a usable anchor (the
# Scala profile hit exactly this).

# Inside a struct type: type LineItem struct > the Taxable field.
# Proves `type` is a real container — the entry the generator never proposed.
# Also the case where type_declaration and type_spec start on the same line and
# the breadcrumb walker must collapse them to one entry, not two.
47

# Inside a conditional inside a method: type LineItem > Taxed > if l.Taxable.
# The method is on a value receiver, the shallowest method chain here.
54

# Inside a range loop inside a conditional inside a method:
# Invoice > Compute > for range > if line.Void().
# The deepest control-flow chain; `continue` is the only one in the file.
98

# Inside a deferred closure inside a conditional inside a method:
# Invoice > Describe > if verbose > defer func().
# Proves a func_literal body is reachable — the landmark no sample can propose.
123

# The deepest named chain: a closure nested in a method, so the trail is
# Invoice > Discount > apply := func(...). This is the line that proves a
# nested `function` lands in the trail alongside `method`.
136
